# the system's error dialog (the game's own network error at its title, with PSN out of reach):
# hidden with agent.errdialog=0 (unattended runs: the system's dialog takes the controller)
sceErrorDialogOpen
sceErrorDialogUpdateStatus
sceErrorDialogGetStatus
sceErrorDialogClose
sceErrorDialogTerminate
# the system's message dialog and save-data dialog: the game opens these on first boot without
# save data (autosave notice, save-data creation) and when save data is missing or corrupt.
# Suppressed like the error dialog: never shown, reported finished immediately.
sceMsgDialogOpen
sceMsgDialogUpdateStatus
sceMsgDialogGetStatus
sceMsgDialogClose
sceMsgDialogTerminate
sceSaveDataDialogOpen
sceSaveDataDialogUpdateStatus
sceSaveDataDialogGetStatus
sceSaveDataDialogClose
sceSaveDataDialogTerminate
# Dead or Alive Xtreme 3 Scarlet's VR mode is gated behind the "VR Passport" add-on, which is
# discontinued and no longer sold; its VR assets ship in the base game. The game learns what it
# owns only through this one call (the only AppContent query it imports); agent.vrunlock reports
# the Passport installed. Off by default; harmless to the other game (which never sets it).
sceAppContentGetAddcontInfoList
sceAppContentAddcontMount
sceAppContentAddcontUnmount
# the game's own files: /app0/NN/package_data.bin served from /data/doax3vr2/port/ (agent.port=1),
# the first /app0/ paths logged
sceKernelOpen
sceKernelStat
sceFiosFHOpen
sceRtcGetCurrentNetworkTick
